    "field": "Climate variability",
    "problem": "The long-standing attribution of climate trends to internal multidecadal oscillations is challenged by the difficulty in distinguishing these signals from random climatic noise or the forced response to external factors like anthropogenic forcing.",
    "method": "The authors use a multi-taper method singular value decomposition (MTM-SVD) signal detection tool on observational data and climate model simulations to test for internal multidecadal and interdecadal oscillatory signals that are statistically distinguishable from the background climatic noise.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze observational data and climate model simulations to determine if there is consistent evidence for internal multidecadal or interdecadal climate oscillations that are distinguishable from background climatic noise.",
