        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Pacific basin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "A substantial body of research has argued for the existence of an oscillatory climate mode centred in the Pacific basin with an interdecadal (~20 year) timescale. This mode is variously referred to as the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation (IPO)3\u20136 or Pacific Decadal Oscillation (PDO)7, arguably two manifestations of the same phenomenon.",
